  "lineage": "Ottoman-Turkish and Arab art-music practice for the end-blown rim-edge reed flute, codified in Mevlevi lodges and Istanbul mesk pedagogy from the 16th-19th centuries and carried into 20th-century state conservatories by players such as Niyazi Sayin and Aka Gunduz Kutbay, marked by unmetered taksim in a single makam, breathy overblown octave leaps, comma-inflected perde tuning, glissando finger-slides and portamento, and the long-breathed ascending-then-descending seyir arc preceding the metered pesrev.",
